<title>FRANCE: Paris postal traffic up 4.5pct in Jan-June.</title>
<headline>Paris postal traffic up 4.5pct in Jan-June.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paris' Charles de Gaulle (CDG) and Orly airports handled 66,899 tonnes of postal traffic in the first six months of 1997, an increase of 4.5 percent on the same period the previous year, the airport authority said.</p>
<p>Dedicated postal traffic flights totalled 4,203, up 11.0 percent on Jan-Jun 1996. These carried 63.0 percent of global postal tonnage compared to 57.4 percent in first half 1996.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
